    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2002-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let the angle be \\(x.\\) Then \\(90 - x = \\dfrac14(180 - x),\\) so \\(360 - 4x = 180 - x.\\)\n\nThis gives \\(3x = 180,\\) so \\(x = 60.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "The complement is \\(90 - x\\) and the supplement is \\(180 - x\\)",
        "Solve \\(90 - x = \\dfrac14(180 - x)\\)"
      ],
